= CSMS User Manual =

The '''CSMS''' (''Central System Management System'') is an [https://www.openchargealliance.org/ OCPP 1.6] Central System for managing and monitoring electric‑vehicle (EV) charging infrastructure. It acts as the backend that charge points connect to over WebSocket, and it provides a web interface for operators to control chargers, track charging sessions, manage RFID authorization, calculate costs, and optimise charging using dynamic electricity tariffs.

This manual describes how to '''install''', '''configure''', and '''use''' the CSMS.

__TOC__

== Overview ==

The CSMS performs the following core functions:

* '''Charge point communication''' — speaks OCPP 1.6 to charge points over WebSocket (default port '''9000''').
* '''Web interface & REST API''' — operator dashboard and JSON API (default port '''9001''').
* '''Session tracking''' — records charging transactions with detailed meter values (energy, power, current per phase, temperature).
* '''RFID authorization''' — manages the whitelist of RFID cards/tags allowed to charge.
* '''Smart charging''' — integrates with [https://www.zonneplan.nl/ Zonneplan] to fetch hourly electricity tariffs and find the cheapest charging window.
* '''Cost calculation''' — computes charging costs from hourly electricity prices (with a configurable default tariff).
* '''Email notifications''' — sends alerts for boot, fault, connect/disconnect, and transaction events.
* '''Event & message logging''' — logs all OCPP messages and system events for auditing and troubleshooting.

=== Architecture ===

<pre>
Charge Point  ──(OCPP / WebSocket :9000)──►  central_system.py  ──►  cs_db.py  ──►  SQLite DB
                                                                                    ▲
Web Browser   ──(HTTP :9001)───────────────►  csms.py (Flask)  ──────────────────────┘

External services:
  Zonneplan API  ──►  hourly electricity tariffs
  SMTP server    ──►  email notifications
</pre>

{| class="wikitable"
! Component !! File !! Responsibility
|-
| Web GUI + REST API || <code>csms.py</code> || Flask web server and JSON endpoints (entry point)
|-
| OCPP server || <code>central_system.py</code> || OCPP 1.6 WebSocket server and message handlers
|-
| Database layer || <code>cs_db.py</code> || SQLite schema and data access
|-
| Email notifications || <code>mail_notify.py</code> || SMTP delivery of event notifications
|-
| Zonneplan integration || <code>zonneplan.py</code> || Login flow and tariff retrieval
|}

== Installation ==

=== Requirements ===

* '''Python 3''' (the application uses f‑strings, type hints, and <code>asyncio</code>).
* Python packages listed in <code>requirements.txt</code>:

{| class="wikitable"
! Package !! Purpose
|-
| <code>flask</code> || Web framework for the UI and REST API
|-
| <code>ocpp</code> || OCPP 1.6 protocol implementation
|-
| <code>websockets</code> || WebSocket server for OCPP connections
|-
| <code>pyyaml</code> || YAML configuration file parsing
|-
| <code>requests</code> || HTTP client for the Zonneplan API
|-
| <code>python-dateutil</code> || Date/time parsing utilities
|}

=== Install steps ===

# Create the application and data directories:
#: <pre>sudo mkdir -p /opt/charger/CSMS /opt/charger/data /var/log/charger</pre>
# Copy the CSMS source files into <code>/opt/charger/CSMS/</code>.
# (Recommended) create a virtual environment and install dependencies:
#: <pre>cd /opt/charger/CSMS
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt</pre>
# Place a configuration file (see [[#Configuration]]) in the CSMS directory, e.g. <code>config_instance1.yaml</code>.

=== Running manually ===

The application is started from <code>csms.py</code>. A configuration file can be supplied with the <code>-c</code> / <code>--config</code> option:

<pre>
python3 csms.py --config /opt/charger/CSMS/config_instance1.yaml
</pre>

If no <code>--config</code> is given, built‑in defaults are used:

{| class="wikitable"
! Setting !! Default
|-
| <code>server_name</code> || <code>"Backend"</code>
|-
| <code>database_path</code> || <code>/opt/charger/data/csms.db</code>
|-
| <code>web_port</code> || <code>9001</code>
|-
| <code>ocpp_port</code> || <code>9000</code>
|}

On first start the database schema is created automatically. Once running, open the web interface at:

: <code>http://&lt;host&gt;:9001</code>

=== Running as a systemd service ===

A service unit is provided (<code>systemd/charger-csms.service</code>):

<pre>
[Unit]
Description=Charger Point Management System (CSMS)
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
WorkingDirectory=/opt/charger/CSMS
ExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 /opt/charger/CSMS/csms.py
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5

StandardOutput=file:/var/log/charger/csms.stdout
StandardError=file:/var/log/charger/csms.stderr

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
</pre>

To install and enable the service:

<pre>
sudo cp systemd/charger-csms.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now charger-csms
</pre>

Useful management commands:

<pre>
sudo systemctl status charger-csms      # check status
sudo systemctl restart charger-csms     # restart
sudo journalctl -u charger-csms -f      # follow logs
</pre>

{{Note|To pass a config file to the service, append <code>--config /opt/charger/CSMS/config_instance1.yaml</code> to the <code>ExecStart</code> line.}}

