=== Managing charge points ===

Charge points connect automatically over OCPP. From the charge point pages you can view connector status, hardware details, and the connection's online/offline state, and you can remove a charger that is no longer in use.

=== Controlling a charging session ===

When a charger is connected over OCPP, the following remote commands are available from its detail page:

* '''Remote Start''' — begin a charging session.
* '''Remote Stop''' — end the active session.
* '''Reset''' — soft or hard reboot of the charger.
* '''Unlock Connector''' — release the charging cable.
* '''Change Availability''' — enable or disable a connector.
* '''Get Configuration''' — query the charger's OCPP configuration keys.

=== Managing RFID cards ===

On the '''RFID''' page you can:

* List all registered cards.
* Add, edit, or delete cards (owner, billing account, blocked flag, optional site restriction).
* '''Bulk import''' multiple RFID records.

When a charger reads an RFID tag, it is validated against this whitelist; blocked cards are rejected.

=== Managing transactions ===

The '''Transactions''' page lists charging sessions with start/stop times, energy delivered, the RFID used, and stop reason. For each session you can:

* View detailed meter values and a charging timeline.
* See an hourly '''cost breakdown''' (when Zonneplan tariffs are available).
* Assign a '''car''' to estimate distance travelled from the energy used.
* Edit or delete the session, or force‑close an active session if needed.

=== Smart charging ===

Using a car profile and the Zonneplan tariff forecast, the CSMS can compute the cheapest charging window. Provide the car, the current battery percentage, and the charging power (kW); the system returns the recommended start/end times and estimated cost. Charging schedules can also be created, edited, and deleted.

