== OCPP Support Reference ==

The CSMS implements the following OCPP 1.6 actions.

=== Messages received from charge points ===

{| class="wikitable"
! Action !! Purpose
|-
| <code>BootNotification</code> || Charger startup info (vendor, model, firmware)
|-
| <code>Heartbeat</code> || Keep‑alive signal
|-
| <code>StatusNotification</code> || Connector status changes (Preparing, Charging, Faulted, etc.)
|-
| <code>Authorize</code> || RFID authorization check
|-
| <code>StartTransaction</code> || Charging session started
|-
| <code>StopTransaction</code> || Charging session ended
|-
| <code>MeterValues</code> || Energy, power, current, and temperature measurements
|-
| <code>DataTransfer</code> || Vendor‑specific messages
|}

=== Commands sent to charge points ===

{| class="wikitable"
! Action !! Purpose
|-
| <code>RemoteStartTransaction</code> || Start a charging session
|-
| <code>RemoteStopTransaction</code> || Stop a charging session
|-
| <code>Reset</code> || Soft/hard reboot
|-
| <code>UnlockConnector</code> || Unlock the connector cable
|-
| <code>ChangeAvailability</code> || Enable/disable a connector
|-
| <code>ChangeConfiguration</code> || Modify a charger setting
|-
| <code>GetConfiguration</code> || Query charger configuration
|-
| <code>TriggerMessage</code> || Request a status or meter update
|-
| <code>ClearCache</code> || Clear the charger's authorization cache
|}

=== Captured meter measurands ===

* <code>Energy.Active.Import.Register</code> — cumulative energy (Wh/kWh)
* <code>Power.Active.Import</code> — instantaneous power (W)
* <code>Current.Import.L1 / L2 / L3</code> — current per phase (A)
* <code>Temperature</code> — charger internal temperature (°C)

== Troubleshooting ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Symptom !! Things to check
|-
| Chargers not connecting || Confirm the charger points to <code>ws://&lt;host&gt;:9000</code> and that the OCPP port matches <code>ocpp_port</code>; check firewall rules.
|-
| Web UI not reachable || Verify the service is running and that <code>web_port</code> (9001) is open.
|-
| No cost data on sessions || Ensure Zonneplan is authenticated and tariffs are being fetched; otherwise the default tariff (€0.30/kWh) is used.
|-
| Emails not sent || Use the '''test email''' button on the Mail Config page; verify SMTP host, port, protocol, and credentials.
|-
| Service won't start || Inspect <code>/var/log/charger/csms.stderr</code> and <code>journalctl -u charger-csms</code>; confirm dependencies are installed and the config path is correct.
|}

== Quick Deployment Checklist ==

# Install Python 3 and run <code>pip install -r requirements.txt</code>.
# Create <code>/opt/charger/CSMS/</code>, <code>/opt/charger/data/</code>, and <code>/var/log/charger/</code>.
# Add a configuration file (e.g. <code>config_instance1.yaml</code>).
# Install and enable the systemd service.
# Open the web UI at <code>http://&lt;host&gt;:9001</code>.
# Confirm the OCPP port (9000) matches your chargers' configuration.
# (Optional) Configure email notifications on the Mail Config page.
# (Optional) Authenticate Zonneplan on the Zonneplan Config page.
